%I A399138 #43 Nov 18 2026 15:58:05
%S A399138 1,8,16,28,40,64
%N A399138 a(n) = maximum number of points in an n X n X n grid with no three collinear.
%C A399138 Collinear means collinear as points of R^3 (not modulo n); cf. A280537 for the "no four coplanar" analog.
%C A399138 Lower bounds for the next terms are a(7) >= 73 (attached witness file) and a(8) >= 94 (Kudriashov's linked 94-point configuration). [Updated by _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 27 2026]
%C A399138 a(p) >= p^2 for every prime p, via the graph of an anisotropic binary quadratic form: {(x, y, Q(x,y) mod p) : 0 <= x,y < p} with Q = x^2 - d*y^2, d a quadratic non-residue, contains no three collinear points. For Q = x^2 + y^2 (which requires p == 3 (mod 4)) this is the construction of Por and Wood.
%C A399138 The maximum size of a connected set of points (with each point connected to its six nearest neighbors), no three collinear, is 26. See A393939. - _Pontus von Brömssen_, Oct 03 2026
%H A399138 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22019279">Certified exact values for the no-three-in-line problem in the three-dimensional grid</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A399138 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="https://github.com/iwasborninbali/oeis-A399138">Witnesses, proof logs and checks</a>, GitHub, 2026.
%H A399138 Aleksei Kudriashov, <a href="/A399138/a399138_1.txt">Witness configurations for a(1)-a(6) (with a second, nonuniform optimum for n = 5) and for the bounds a(7) >= 73, a(8) >= 94, a(9) >= 116, a(10) >= 138, a(11) >= 164</a>
%H A399138 OEIS Wiki, <a href="https://oeis.org/wiki/A400K_Winners">A400K Winners</a>, 2026.
%H A399138 Ed Pegg, <a href="https://community.wolfram.com/t/the-min-and-max-of-the-no-3-in-line-problem/27121">The Min and Max of the No-3-in-line problem</a>, Wolfram Community, 2026.
%H A399138 A. Por and D. R. Wood, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s00453-006-0158-9">No-Three-in-Line-in-3D</a>, Algorithmica 47 (2007), 481-488.
%H A399138 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/No-Three-in-a-LineProblem.html">No-Three-in-a-Line Problem</a>.
%F A399138 a(n) = Theta(n^2): the upper bound a(n) <= 2*n^2 is elementary (each of the n^2 axis-parallel lines carries at most two points; attained at n = 2), the lower bound Omega(n^2) is due to Por and Wood.
%e A399138 a(2) = 8: all eight points of the 2 X 2 X 2 cube may be taken, since no line contains three points of that grid.
%Y A399138 Cf. A000769 (the two-dimensional problem), A280537 (no four coplanar in the same grid), A157882, A393939.
%K A399138 nonn,more,hard,nice,changed
%O A399138 1,2
